WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.573 --> 00:00:18.714
Several trolls were waiting when Morb arrived back at the fortress.

2
00:00:19.455 --> 00:00:22.856
The leader, an especially large and ugly troll, grunted.

3
00:00:23.536 --> 00:00:29.019
A fuzzy image of a figure trapped behind iron bars appeared briefly above his head before quickly fading

4
00:00:29.139 --> 00:00:31.920
out. Morb tried to hide his disdain.

5
00:00:32.672 --> 00:00:37.154
Trolls were disgusting creatures, with their rough magic and rougher appetites.

6
00:00:37.854 --> 00:00:39.755
But he needed them, at least for now.

7
00:00:40.776 --> 00:00:41.996
"Prepare the treatment!"

8
00:00:42.417 --> 00:00:43.257
he ordered the troll.

9
00:00:44.017 --> 00:00:45.198
The troll lumbered off.

10
00:00:46.158 --> 00:00:49.960
Morb strode across the room and down a steep stone stairwell.

11
00:00:52.701 --> 00:00:54.522
At the bottom was a heavy wooden door.

12
00:00:55.302 --> 00:00:58.524
As soon as he pushed it open, the prisoners began crying out.

13
00:00:59.156 --> 00:01:03.358
There were now more than a dozen of them in the cells, peering out from behind the heavy

14
00:01:03.518 --> 00:01:04.198
iron bars.

15
00:01:05.219 --> 00:01:07.199
But Morb barely looked at most of them.

16
00:01:07.539 --> 00:01:10.461
His eyes went directly to one particular cell.

17
00:01:11.021 --> 00:01:14.342
The long-nosed old man inside stared back defiantly.

18
00:01:15.102 --> 00:01:18.484
His hands and legs were tied so he couldn't move without falling over.

19
00:01:18.764 --> 00:01:21.385
But he stood tall and proud despite the restraints.

20
00:01:21.405 --> 00:01:25.207
"You!" Boz spat out as Morb approached.

21
00:01:25.227 --> 00:01:28.508
"I should have guessed when I heard the news.

22
00:01:29.288 --> 00:01:33.330
You never could accept that you weren't meant to—" "Silence!"

23
00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:34.670
Morb cut him off.

24
00:01:34.991 --> 00:01:36.211
He turned toward the door.

25
00:01:36.231 --> 00:01:37.572
"I'm ready!"

26
00:01:37.952 --> 00:01:38.872
he called loudly.

27
00:01:39.873 --> 00:01:41.914
Heavy footsteps tromped down the stairs.

28
00:01:42.614 --> 00:01:46.175
A pair of trolls came in, lugging an iron cauldron between them.

29
00:01:46.856 --> 00:01:49.317
The prisoners shrank back fearfully when they saw it.

30
00:01:49.737 --> 00:01:50.637
All except Boz.

31
00:01:51.418 --> 00:01:53.299
"What are you going to do, Morb?"

32
00:01:53.659 --> 00:01:54.199
he demanded.

33
00:01:54.219 --> 00:01:56.260
"Feed me to your pet trolls?

34
00:01:57.044 --> 00:01:59.786
The Red Council will hear about this, have no doubt.

35
00:02:00.867 --> 00:02:07.051
Using Flash Freezes and Dousing spells, holding people prisoner You won't get away with it!"

36
00:02:08.212 --> 00:02:09.092
Morb ignored him.

37
00:02:09.413 --> 00:02:11.994
The trolls tipped the cauldron, spilling its contents.

38
00:02:12.795 --> 00:02:16.137
Leeches. Dozens of enormous pale blue leeches.

39
00:02:16.898 --> 00:02:18.559
Their faces turned this way and that.

40
00:02:19.179 --> 00:02:22.462
They could sense the powerful magic of all the Red prisoners nearby.

41
00:02:22.482 --> 00:02:25.544
"Get Boz," Morb said.

42
00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:29.822
The leeches slowly wriggled between the bars and into Boz's cell.

43
00:02:30.823 --> 00:02:31.903
Boz looked startled.

44
00:02:32.323 --> 00:02:34.024
"Where did those things come from?"

45
00:02:34.525 --> 00:02:35.125
he exclaimed.

46
00:02:36.045 --> 00:02:38.827
"There are no leeches that size anywhere in Magica!

47
00:02:39.247 --> 00:02:40.708
How did you—ahh!"

48
00:02:41.488 --> 00:02:44.790
The rest of his words were lost as the leeches slithered up his legs.

49
00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:50.173
Their pale bodies brightened to a vivid electric blue as they fed on Boz's magic.

50
00:02:51.173 --> 00:02:53.915
Morb watched for a moment, enjoying the sight.

51
00:02:54.675 --> 00:02:55.536
Then he turned away.

52
00:02:56.268 --> 00:03:00.310
He still had unfinished business to deal with before he could put the rest of his plan into

53
00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:07.153
motion. He hurried back upstairs, pulled out the picture he'd taken from Boz's house, and carefully ripped out

54
00:03:07.213 --> 00:03:08.033
the boy's face.

55
00:03:08.933 --> 00:03:13.735
Morb then stepped toward the Secret Eye, his gaze on the ancient skull at the top.

56
00:03:14.676 --> 00:03:16.237
Then he noticed a flutter of movement.

57
00:03:16.857 --> 00:03:20.879
Turning his head, he saw an insect hovering just outside the window.

58
00:03:20.899 --> 00:03:23.180
"A spy fly!"

59
00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:24.020
he murmured.

60
00:03:24.724 --> 00:03:27.545
"Now who would want to spy on little old me?"

61
00:03:28.325 --> 00:03:30.306
The spy fly sensed it had been spotted.

62
00:03:30.606 --> 00:03:31.926
It spun around to fly off.

63
00:03:32.586 --> 00:03:34.287
But Morb was too quick for it.

64
00:03:34.967 --> 00:03:39.348
Rubbing his fingers together, he blew it to pieces with an extra-strong Flash Freeze.

65
00:03:42.189 --> 00:03:46.510
Then he gently placed the Red boy's picture into one of the skull's eye sockets.

66
00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:51.731
Stepping back, he watched as the map above slowly started to change.

67
00:03:51.751 --> 00:03:55.185
"Stay here," Zann ordered Zing.

68
00:03:55.565 --> 00:03:56.585
"We'll be back soon."

69
00:03:57.426 --> 00:03:58.827
The dragon spat fire at him.

70
00:03:59.207 --> 00:04:00.087
Zann rolled his eyes.

71
00:04:00.107 --> 00:04:03.889
"Let me talk to him."

72
00:04:04.570 --> 00:04:05.970
Darb knelt in front of Zing.

73
00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:07.271
"Listen, buddy.

74
00:04:07.551 --> 00:04:10.213
We need you to guard the cave while we check on Gliss, okay?"

75
00:04:11.133 --> 00:04:13.274
Zing continued to look skeptical for a second.

76
00:04:14.275 --> 00:04:17.677
Then finally he whistled happily, wriggling his whole body.

77
00:04:18.437 --> 00:04:19.217
Zann sighed.

78
00:04:19.538 --> 00:04:21.919
The dragon never could resist Darb's charms.

79
00:04:22.699 --> 00:04:23.700
It was kind of annoying.

80
00:04:24.424 --> 00:04:27.006
"Let's go," Perda said, grabbing Darb's hand.

81
00:04:27.026 --> 00:04:28.608
"I've got Darb."

82
00:04:28.628 --> 00:04:31.290
"Meet you in Gliss' living room."

83
00:04:31.671 --> 00:04:33.933
Zann closed his eyes, focusing his mind.

84
00:04:34.633 --> 00:04:36.475
This was no time to be sloppy.

85
00:04:37.355 --> 00:04:39.137
He'd been in Gliss' house several times.

86
00:04:39.838 --> 00:04:41.599
Her parents were always inviting him over.

87
00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:44.001
It was actually a little embarrassing.

88
00:04:44.282 --> 00:04:48.485
They seemed to think that because Zann and Gliss were the only two Reds in their level, they

89
00:04:48.505 --> 00:04:49.206
should be friends.

90
00:04:49.967 --> 00:04:51.348
Maybe even more than friends.

91
00:04:52.324 --> 00:04:54.326
Zann tried not to get distracted by that.

92
00:04:54.946 --> 00:04:58.089
He and Gliss weren't especially close, but he liked her fine.

93
00:04:58.889 --> 00:05:02.112
He definitely didn't want to see her captured by this Morb character.

94
00:05:02.132 --> 00:05:04.874
"Zap," he whispered.

95
00:05:07.696 --> 00:05:11.780
Bam! He landed hard on the ground with the wind knocked out of him.

96
00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:14.682
Opening his eyes, he saw Gliss' house.

97
00:05:14.702 --> 00:05:18.125
"Oof!" Perda grunted beside him.

98
00:05:18.805 --> 00:05:21.948
She and Darb appeared, both of them also flung off their feet.

99
00:05:22.896 --> 00:05:23.717
"What happened?"

100
00:05:24.017 --> 00:05:24.617
Darb asked.

101
00:05:25.358 --> 00:05:26.699
Zann stood up, wincing.

102
00:05:26.719 --> 00:05:28.700
"They must have a Shield spell up."

103
00:05:29.501 --> 00:05:31.042
"No wonder," Perda said.

104
00:05:31.062 --> 00:05:33.283
"They're probably worried about the warning.

105
00:05:33.984 --> 00:05:36.005
But it means we're blocked out too."

106
00:05:36.025 --> 00:05:38.327
"No big deal," Darb said.

107
00:05:38.347 --> 00:05:41.929
"It is possible to get into a house without using magic, you know."

108
00:05:42.249 --> 00:05:42.789
He smiled.

109
00:05:42.810 --> 00:05:44.791
"It's called knocking on the door."

110
00:05:44.811 --> 00:05:50.134
"Zann!" Gliss' mother exclaimed when she answered the door.

111
00:05:50.154 --> 00:05:52.256
"You shouldn't be out right now.

112
00:05:52.692 --> 00:05:53.773
Haven't you heard the news?"

113
00:05:54.574 --> 00:05:56.455
She quickly ushered all the kids inside.

114
00:05:57.196 --> 00:05:59.117
Her husband and Gliss were in the main room.

115
00:05:59.137 --> 00:06:00.798
"You're okay!"

116
00:06:01.139 --> 00:06:03.140
Perda exclaimed, rushing over to Gliss.

117
00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:06.062
"Listen," Zann told Gliss' parents.

118
00:06:06.403 --> 00:06:08.745
"We just figured out who's behind all the trouble."

119
00:06:08.765 --> 00:06:10.106
"You did?"

120
00:06:10.386 --> 00:06:11.246
Gliss' father said.

121
00:06:11.266 --> 00:06:12.607
"I'll show you."

122
00:06:13.048 --> 00:06:15.290
Zann snapped his fingers to call up the Directory.

123
00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:18.192
"Morb," he said when the book appeared.

124
00:06:18.956 --> 00:06:22.781
But before the image could fully form, there was a sudden, blinding flash.

125
00:06:23.482 --> 00:06:27.307
The next thing Zann knew, a familiar figure was standing before him.

126
00:06:28.248 --> 00:06:29.269
"You called?"

127
00:06:29.690 --> 00:06:31.091
Morb said with a sneer.
